IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`
IMPORT `roc7-order-28`
IMPORT `roc7-order-30`
IMPORT `roc7-order-33a`
IMPORT `roc7-order-33b`
IMPORT `roc7-order-33c`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- DUTIES WITH A FIXED TIME LIMIT, WRITTEN AS REGULATIVE RULES (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ... LEST BREACH).  LAYER 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- Written with a macro builder that quotes the source lines and writes the @ref; the builder is not part of this row, so edit this file directly.
--
-- Each rule below states one duty of the text with its time limit in DAYS, counted from 0 at the event the text names.
-- The text names no consequence of breach in these rules, so the consequence is the bare BREACH, with the text's own words as the reason.
-- Each rule has a decision-function twin in the module that holds its Order, which carries the same period as a Period constant
-- and answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` over the last day the party states (O 3 r 3 counts the days).  The twin is asserted in roc7-tests-duties.l4.
-- A #TRACE result is an Information diagnostic, not an assertion: it is run on both main builds and recorded in NOTES.md.

DECLARE `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` IS ONE OF
    `o 33 r 2(4) the defendant served in Singapore`
    `o 33 r 2(5) the defendant served out of Singapore`
    `o 33 r 5(1)(b) the caveator's solicitor`
    `o 33 r 18(9) each party to the collision action`
    `o 33 r 20(3) the party who has served a list of electronic track data`
    `o 30 r 5(2) the person notified of the hearing of the Reference`
    `o 33 r 41(5) the claiming party`
    `o 33 r 22(2)(c) the Sheriff`

DECLARE `o 33 r 2(4) duty act` IS ONE OF
    `o 33 r 2(4) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest`
    `o 33 r 2(5) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest out of Singapore`
    `o 33 r 5(1)(b) give bail or pay the amount specified into Court`
    `o 33 r 18(9) serve a copy of the party's preliminary act on every other party`
    `o 33 r 20(3) allow inspection and copying of the electronic track data`
    `o 30 r 5(2) inform the Tribunal in writing of the intention to be heard`
    `o 33 r 41(5) enter the reference for hearing by lodging a Request`
    `o 33 r 22(2)(c) send the notice for publication in the Gazette`

-- src:4586 | (4) A defendant who is served an originating claim in Singapore must file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest within 14 days after the originating claim is served on the defendant.
@ref O 33 r 2(4) duty (src:4586)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 33 r 2(4) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(4) the defendant served in Singapore`
    MUST `o 33 r 2(4) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 33 r 2(4) the defendant served in Singapore` BECAUSE "no notice of intention to contest or not contest was filed and served within 14 days of service in Singapore"

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(4) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(4) the defendant served in Singapore` DOES `o 33 r 2(4) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest` AT 1

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(4) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(4) the defendant served in Singapore` DOES `o 33 r 2(4) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest` AT 14

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(4) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(4) the defendant served in Singapore` DOES `o 33 r 2(4) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest` AT 15

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(4) duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- src:4587 | (5) A defendant who is served out of Singapore must file and serve such a notice within 21 days after the originating claim is served on the defendant.
@ref O 33 r 2(5) duty (src:4587)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 33 r 2(5) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(5) the defendant served out of Singapore`
    MUST `o 33 r 2(5) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest out of Singapore`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 33 r 2(5) the defendant served out of Singapore` BECAUSE "no notice of intention to contest or not contest was filed and served within 21 days of service out of Singapore"

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(5) the defendant served out of Singapore` DOES `o 33 r 2(5) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest out of Singapore` AT 1

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(5) the defendant served out of Singapore` DOES `o 33 r 2(5) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest out of Singapore` AT 21

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 2(5) the defendant served out of Singapore` DOES `o 33 r 2(5) file and serve the notice of intention to contest or not contest out of Singapore` AT 22

#TRACE `o 33 r 2(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 22)

-- src:4636 | ( b )
-- src:4637 | within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun, to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court,
-- src:4638 | and the caveat so filed must be entered in the record of caveats.
@ref O 33 r 5(1)(b) duty (src:4636-4638)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 33 r 5(1)(b) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 33 r 5(1)(b) the caveator's solicitor`
    MUST `o 33 r 5(1)(b) give bail or pay the amount specified into Court`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 33 r 5(1)(b) the caveator's solicitor` BECAUSE "bail was not given and the amount was not paid into Court within 3 days after notice of the action"

#TRACE `o 33 r 5(1)(b) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 5(1)(b) the caveator's solicitor` DOES `o 33 r 5(1)(b) give bail or pay the amount specified into Court` AT 1

#TRACE `o 33 r 5(1)(b) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 5(1)(b) the caveator's solicitor` DOES `o 33 r 5(1)(b) give bail or pay the amount specified into Court` AT 3

#TRACE `o 33 r 5(1)(b) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 5(1)(b) the caveator's solicitor` DOES `o 33 r 5(1)(b) give bail or pay the amount specified into Court` AT 4

#TRACE `o 33 r 5(1)(b) duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 4)

-- src:4823 | (9) Within 14 days after the last preliminary act in the action is filed, each party must serve on every other party a copy of the firstmentioned party’s preliminary act.
@ref O 33 r 18(9) duty (src:4823)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 33 r 18(9) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 33 r 18(9) each party to the collision action`
    MUST `o 33 r 18(9) serve a copy of the party's preliminary act on every other party`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 33 r 18(9) each party to the collision action` BECAUSE "the copy of the preliminary act was not served within 14 days after the last preliminary act was filed"

#TRACE `o 33 r 18(9) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 18(9) each party to the collision action` DOES `o 33 r 18(9) serve a copy of the party's preliminary act on every other party` AT 1

#TRACE `o 33 r 18(9) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 18(9) each party to the collision action` DOES `o 33 r 18(9) serve a copy of the party's preliminary act on every other party` AT 14

#TRACE `o 33 r 18(9) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 18(9) each party to the collision action` DOES `o 33 r 18(9) serve a copy of the party's preliminary act on every other party` AT 15

#TRACE `o 33 r 18(9) duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- src:4841 | (3) A party that has served a list of documents under paragraph (2) must, if that party has any electronic track data in the possession, custody or power of that party, allow any other party to inspect, and to take copies of, that electronic track data within 14 days after a request by that other party to do so.
@ref O 33 r 20(3) duty (src:4841)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 33 r 20(3) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 33 r 20(3) the party who has served a list of electronic track data`
    MUST `o 33 r 20(3) allow inspection and copying of the electronic track data`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 33 r 20(3) the party who has served a list of electronic track data` BECAUSE "inspection of the electronic track data was not allowed within 14 days after the request"

#TRACE `o 33 r 20(3) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 20(3) the party who has served a list of electronic track data` DOES `o 33 r 20(3) allow inspection and copying of the electronic track data` AT 1

#TRACE `o 33 r 20(3) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 20(3) the party who has served a list of electronic track data` DOES `o 33 r 20(3) allow inspection and copying of the electronic track data` AT 14

#TRACE `o 33 r 20(3) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 20(3) the party who has served a list of electronic track data` DOES `o 33 r 20(3) allow inspection and copying of the electronic track data` AT 15

#TRACE `o 33 r 20(3) duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- src:4494 | 5. —(1) The Tribunal may direct that any person interested or, where there is a class of persons interested, any one or more persons as representatives of that class, must be notified of the hearing of any Reference and those persons are entitled to be heard following that. (2) If such person desires to be heard in the Reference, the person must within 7 days of the notification inform the Tribunal in writing of the person’s intention to be heard.
@ref O 30 r 5(2) duty (src:4494)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 30 r 5(2) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 30 r 5(2) the person notified of the hearing of the Reference`
    MUST `o 30 r 5(2) inform the Tribunal in writing of the intention to be heard`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 30 r 5(2) the person notified of the hearing of the Reference` BECAUSE "the Tribunal was not informed in writing within 7 days of the notification"

#TRACE `o 30 r 5(2) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 30 r 5(2) the person notified of the hearing of the Reference` DOES `o 30 r 5(2) inform the Tribunal in writing of the intention to be heard` AT 1

#TRACE `o 30 r 5(2) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 30 r 5(2) the person notified of the hearing of the Reference` DOES `o 30 r 5(2) inform the Tribunal in writing of the intention to be heard` AT 7

#TRACE `o 30 r 5(2) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 30 r 5(2) the person notified of the hearing of the Reference` DOES `o 30 r 5(2) inform the Tribunal in writing of the intention to be heard` AT 8

#TRACE `o 30 r 5(2) duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)

-- src:5021 | (5) Not later than 14 days after an appointment for the hearing of a reference has been made, the claiming party or, where the reference is in a limitation action, the claimant must enter the reference for hearing by lodging in the Registry a Request requesting the entry of the reference in the list for hearing on the day appointed.
@ref O 33 r 41(5) duty (src:5021)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 33 r 41(5) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 33 r 41(5) the claiming party`
    MUST `o 33 r 41(5) enter the reference for hearing by lodging a Request`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 33 r 41(5) the claiming party` BECAUSE "the Request was not lodged within 14 days after the appointment for the hearing"

#TRACE `o 33 r 41(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 41(5) the claiming party` DOES `o 33 r 41(5) enter the reference for hearing by lodging a Request` AT 1

#TRACE `o 33 r 41(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 41(5) the claiming party` DOES `o 33 r 41(5) enter the reference for hearing by lodging a Request` AT 14

#TRACE `o 33 r 41(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 41(5) the claiming party` DOES `o 33 r 41(5) enter the reference for hearing by lodging a Request` AT 15

#TRACE `o 33 r 41(5) duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- src:4883 | that within 14 days after the date of payment into Court of the proceeds of sale, the Sheriff must send for publication in the Gazette and such newspaper or publication (if any) as the Court may direct, a notice complying with paragraph (3).
@ref O 33 r 22(2)(c) duty (src:4883)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 33 r 2(4) duty actor` `o 33 r 2(4) duty act`
`o 33 r 22(2)(c) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 33 r 22(2)(c) the Sheriff`
    MUST `o 33 r 22(2)(c) send the notice for publication in the Gazette`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 33 r 22(2)(c) the Sheriff` BECAUSE "the notice was not sent for publication within 14 days after the payment into Court of the proceeds of sale"

#TRACE `o 33 r 22(2)(c) duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 33 r 22(2)(c) the Sheriff` DOES `o 33 r 22(2)(c) send the notice for publication in the Gazette` AT 1

#TRACE `o 33 r 22(2)(c) duty` AT 0 WITH
